<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Landry, Count of Nevers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1028</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Landry of Nevers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Landry, Count of Nevers, was a Burgundian noble who received the county of Nevers around 990 from his father-in-law Otto-William, count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>. He founded the first hereditary dynasty of counts of Nevers and also won the county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auxerre">Auxerre</a>. His descendants held Nevers, Auxerre and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tonnerre">Tonnerre</a>, forming one of the largest lordships of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p></div>
